lg:PL-PP-art27-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "a10a7db3f17463fd75485d73724c19f4b8a18297f626263c3340ac459c3c56a3" ;
    lgo:text """1. On each copy of periodical publications, agency services and other similar press publications, the following shall be given in a visible and customary place:
1) the name and address of the publisher or other competent body,
2) the address of the editorial office and the name of the editor-in-chief,
3) the place and date of issue,
4) the name of the establishment producing the given press publication,
5) the symbol of the authority granting the publication permit, in the cases specified in the provisions on the control of publications and performances,
6) the international standard identifier,
7) the current numbering."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:PL-PP-art27-1-q1 .

lg:PL-PP-art27-2-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "595f89ac966fd93da735cc72f79593172d5e28ee6baedbcbcd9517b79b7950b8" ;
    lgo:text "2. Paragraph 1 applies mutatis mutandis to radio and television recordings and newsreels."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:PL-PP-art27-2-q1 .

lg:PL-PP-art7-2-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "8d6dd6beb985154271a467770e8dfe05677c8677968eda9aee487f1f2192173f" ;
    lgo:text """2. Within the meaning of the Act:
1) the press means periodical publications which do not form a closed, homogeneous whole, appearing not less frequently than once a year, bearing a permanent title or name, a current number and a date, and in particular: newspapers and magazines, agency services, regular telex transmissions, bulletins, radio and television programmes and newsreels; the press also includes all existing and emerging means of mass communication created by technical progress, including plant radio and television broadcasting stations, disseminating periodical publications by means of print, vision, sound or other distribution techniques; the press also covers groups of people and individual persons engaged in journalistic activity,
2) a newspaper is a general-information periodical publication or a transmission by means of sound and of sound and vision, appearing more frequently than once a week,
3) a magazine is a periodical publication appearing not more frequently than once a week and not less frequently than once a year; this provision applies mutatis mutandis to a transmission by means of sound and of sound and vision other than that specified in point 2,
4) press material is any published text or image of an informative, journalistic, documentary or other character submitted for publication in the press, regardless of the means of transmission, kind, form, purpose or authorship,
5) a journalist is a person engaged in editing, creating or preparing press materials, being in an employment relationship with an editorial office or engaged in such activity on behalf of and with the authorisation of an editorial office,
6) an editor is a journalist who decides or co-decides on the publication of press materials,
7) an editor-in-chief is a person having the authority to decide on the overall activity of the editorial office,
8) an editorial office is a unit organising the process of preparing (collecting, evaluating and processing) materials for publication in the press."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:PL-PP-art7-2-q1 .

lg:PL-PP-title-94151b76fc03-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
